    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1333">

                <pb facs="1450" n="1440" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg1440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860H. 48/12–1544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        United States Political Adviser on the Staff of the Supreme Allied
                        Commander, Mediterranean Theater</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-20T19:00:00-04:00">December 20,
                            1944—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>494. Department is in agreement with the position taken by you as stated in your
                    no. 1774 of December 15. We feel that any discussions <pb facs="1451" n="1441"
                        xml:id="pg1441"/> or negotiations with the Yugoslavs should be conducted at
                    some appropriate place where competent US and British representatives can
                    participate. We are still opposed to any relaxation of our stand with respect to
                    observers. We assume that if SACMED is unable to obtain an agreement along the
                    lines specified by the CCS he will, in accordance with his instructions, so
                    advise the CCS.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
